-/// RAII form of `cppgc::subtle::NoGarbageCollectionScope`.
-///
-/// While at least one scope is held, *cppgc-initiated* garbage collections
-/// (allocation-triggered cppgc GCs, `CppHeap::CollectGarbageForTesting`,
-/// finalization of an incremental cppgc GC) are deferred. It does **not**
-/// prevent V8's own GCs from finalizing an attached CppHeap: in the unified
-/// heap, a V8 major GC still marks and sweeps cppgc objects (observed in the
-/// cppgc spike, item 1). Combine with [`DisallowGarbageCollectionScope`] and
-/// keep the owning thread from triggering V8 GCs if you need "no finalization".
-/// Marking may continue inside the scope.
